# GraphQL

- Apollo Server stays at `/graphql` on the BFF port. Express there only hosts that route. Do not add a REST quote API. Only `apps/web` calls it. Ports are in the Node.js rule.
- Keep the `health` query. One quote mutation is enough.
- GraphQL types follow `@commission-quote/contracts`. Do not declare those fields again.
- Validate variables with the shared schema before the vendor call.
- A vendor body missing `quoteId`, `commissionRate`, or `totalCommission` is an error, not a quote.
- Errors stay short. What must stay out of them is in the security rule.

```graphql
# Bad — secret is an argument; error echoes the vendor
type Query {
  quote(apiKey: String!): Quote
}

# Good — health stays; one mutation; secrets stay on the server
type Query {
  health: String!
}
type Mutation {
  generateQuote(input: QuoteInput!): Quote!
}
```
